`lib/WWW/MailboxOrg/Role/RPC.pm`:

    sub _rpc {
        my ($self, $method, @params) = @_;
        my $client = $self->client or croak "No client set";
        return $client->call($method, @params);
    }

The file uses `croak` but never loads Carp (`use Moo::Role;` does not export it). The module compiles, because the call is only resolved at runtime: as soon as a controller has no client, the caller gets

    Undefined subroutine &WWW::MailboxOrg::Role::RPC::croak called

instead of the intended "No client set".

Done when: the module loads Carp (or Carp::croak) explicitly and a test covers the path without a client, expecting the message "No client set". The test has to be red against the current lib/.


